<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croats</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Croats are a South Slavic people whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> lies in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>. Croatia was linked to the Hungarian crown and later formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands. Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, the Croats were among the nationalities left in a subordinate position by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a>, contributing to the empire's nationality problem.</p></div>
